You are a senior review consolidator. Multiple independent reviewers have scored the same generated code.
Synthesize their feedback into a single consensus review.

## Original Prompt

Write a TypeScript program
that performs CRUD operations on items in an Azure Cosmos DB NoSQL container:
1. Create a CosmosClient using endpoint and key
2. Create a database "TestDB" and container "Items" with partition key "/category"
3. Create an item with properties: id, category, name, quantity
4. Read the item back using item().read()
5. Query items where category equals "electronics" using parameterized query
6. Replace the item with updated quantity using item().replace()
7. Delete the item using item().delete()

Show required npm package and handle errors with appropriate status code checks.

## Individual Reviews

### Reviewer 1 (claude-opus-4.6)
```json
{
  "model": "claude-opus-4.6",
  "scores": {
    "criteria": [
      {
        "name": "Code Builds",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Static analysis confirms all imports (StatusCodes, CosmosClient, Database, Container) are valid exports of @azure/cosmos v4.9.3. tsconfig.json is properly configured. noUnusedLocals is commented out so unused Database/Container imports won't error. Code is syntactically valid TypeScript."
      },
      {
        "name": "Latest Package Versions",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "@azure/cosmos 4.9.3 matches the latest version on npm. TypeScript 6.0.3 and @types/node 25.6.0 are current."
      },
      {
        "name": "Best Practices",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Uses key-based authentication (endpoint + key) instead of DefaultAzureCredential or other identity-based auth. Does not use @azure/logger for diagnostics."
      },
      {
        "name": "Error Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Catch block casts error to a generic object {code, message} rather than checking for RestError from @azure/core-rest-pipeline. RestError is re-exported from @azure/cosmos but not used. No retry logic."
      },
      {
        "name": "Code Quality",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Clean, well-structured code with clear comments matching each step. Good use of TypeScript interfaces, destructuring, and status code checks on individual operations."
      },
      {
        "name": "Correct @azure/ Scoped Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses @azure/cosmos which is the correct scoped package. No deprecated unscoped packages."
      },
      {
        "name": "@azure/identity for Authentication",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Does not include @azure/identity as a dependency. Uses endpoint + key (master key) for authentication. No DefaultAzureCredential or any Entra token credential."
      },
      {
        "name": "Client Constructor with Endpoint and Credential",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "CosmosClient is constructed with { endpoint, key } instead of { endpoint, aadCredentials } with a credential object from @azure/identity."
      },
      {
        "name": "Async/Await Pattern",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All asynchronous operations use async/await. Entry point is an async main() function with .catch(). No .then()/.catch() chains or callback patterns."
      },
      {
        "name": "Pagination with for-await-of",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Query uses .fetchAll() which loads all results into memory at once. Should use for-await-of over the QueryIterator (which is an AsyncIterable) instead of fetchAll()."
      },
      {
        "name": "LRO Pattern (beginXxx + pollUntilDone)",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Not applicable — Cosmos DB CRUD operations (create, read, replace, delete) are not long-running operations. No LRO pattern needed."
      },
      {
        "name": "RestError Exception Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Does not catch RestError (which is re-exported from @azure/cosmos). Instead casts to a generic {code, message} object. No statusCode-based error branching in the catch block."
      },
      {
        "name": "No Deprecated Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All dependencies (@azure/cosmos, @types/node, typescript) are current packages with no deprecated or legacy Azure packages."
      },
      {
        "name": "Logging via @azure/logger",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Does not import or use @azure/logger. Does not call setLogLevel() or reference AZURE_LOG_LEVEL environment variable for SDK diagnostic logging."
      },
      {
        "name": "package.json with Correct Dependencies",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Includes valid package.json with @azure/cosmos, tsconfig.json with proper configuration, @types/node for type definitions, and TypeScript 6.0.3."
      },
      {
        "name": "@azure/cosmos npm package",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses @azure/cosmos v4.9.3 as the primary dependency."
      },
      {
        "name": "CosmosClient constructor with endpoint and key",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Creates CosmosClient with { endpoint, key } matching the prompt requirement."
      },
      {
        "name": "createIfNotExists for database and container",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses client.databases.createIfNotExists({ id: 'TestDB' }) and database.containers.createIfNotExists({ id: 'Items', partitionKey: { paths: ['/category'] } })."
      },
      {
        "name": "container.items.create() and item().read()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Creates item with container.items.create(newItem) and reads with container.item(id, category).read\u003cItem\u003e()."
      },
      {
        "name": "container.items.query() with SqlQuerySpec",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses parameterized SqlQuerySpec with query string and parameters array for the category filter."
      },
      {
        "name": "container.item().replace() and .delete()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Replaces with container.item(id, category).replace\u003cItem\u003e(updatedItem) and deletes with container.item(id, category).delete()."
      },
      {
        "name": "FeedResponse iteration and error status codes",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses fetchAll() which returns FeedResponse, iterates over resources array, and checks StatusCodes (Created, Ok, NoContent) on all CRUD operations."
      }
    ]
  },
  "overall_score": 14,
